			"difficulty": "intermediate",
			"estimated_time": "30-40 minutes",
			"learning_objectives": [
				"Self-similarity: the whole contains copies of itself",
				"Fractal dimension: D = log(N)/log(S) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d between integers",
				"Recursion as emergence: simple rules, infinite complexity",
				"Edge of chaos: Mandelbrot boundary, Julia variations",
				"Natural fractals: trees, coastlines, romanesco"
			],
			"content": [
				"Fractals_1: Recursion Introduction \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the function that calls itself",
				"Fractals_2: Recursive Trees \u00e2\u20ac\u201d branching structures, deterministic vs stochastic",
				"Fractals_3: Cantor Set \u00e2\u20ac\u201d infinite subdivision, existence without extension",
				"Fractals_4: Koch Curve \u00e2\u20ac\u201d infinite perimeter enclosing finite area",
				"Fractals_5: Sierpinski \u00e2\u20ac\u201d triangles and pyramids, D \u00e2\u2030\u02c6 1.585",
				"Fractals_6: Menger Sponge \u00e2\u20ac\u201d walkable 3D fractal, D \u00e2\u2030\u02c6 2.727",
